To restart mbatchd:-
badmin mbdrestart

To check status:-
badmin hist
badmin showstatus

To restart sbatchd:-
badmin hrestart <host-name>
Eg: "badmin hrestart lsf-master"

To check sbatchd status:-
lsf_daemons status


# To stop sbd, res and lim seperately ( SEQUENCE IS IMPORTANT )
bctrld stop sbd lsf-master
bctrld stop res lsf-master
bctrld stop lim lsf-master

# To start sbd, res and lim seperately ( SEQUENCE IS IMPORTANT )

While starting lim if you get below error:-
lsfadmin@lsf-master:~$ bctrld start lim lsf-master
Sep  7 12:03:59 2026 6877 4 10.1 setAdmins: root is defined as an administrator. This is not recommended.
Cannot start <lim> because bctrld does not have the setuid bit. To enable the setuid bit, run 'chmod u+s' on the bctrld binary file, or run the 'hostsetup --setuid' command.

Run: "chmod u+s /opt/ibm/lsfsuite/lsf/10.1/linux3.10-glibc2.17-x86_64/bin/bctrld"
and then start lim, but still I got some issues finally I used below command:-

lsf_daemons start
